  "term": "urbanism",
  "definition": "Urbanism here refers to a pattern of settlement centered on small fortified towns within interconnected walled oases, with organized residential, decision-making, and burial areas linked by streets. In this source, it is described as a low or slow form of urbanization that reflects modest but growing social complexity.",
